Yorikiri!

45
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:21,910
Kawamacho!

46
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:24,640
Are you all right?

47
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:26,790
My lady.

48
00:03:27,060 --> 00:03:28,413
It happened so quickly.

49
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:29,442
I couldn't see.

50
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:33,360
No need to worry about me, Lady Hiyori.

51
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:36,147
Though I fear more
enemies may be on the way.

52
00:03:36,620 --> 00:03:38,149
Let's get out of the open.

53
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:39,840
Yes, of course.

54
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:42,680
Hop on my back.

55
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:44,645
It's hard to walk in the snow.

56
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:46,880
Stop that.

57
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:48,649
Is this a joke, Kawamatsu?

58
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:49,860
I'm no child.

59
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:52,380
So you say.

60
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:56,437
But I've never seen an adult pout and
puff out their cheeks like a blowfish.

61
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:58,200
Oh, you're awful!

62
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:02,800
It brings back memories, doesn't it?

63
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:07,240
I never dared to dream that we'd
be walking side by side again.

64
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:09,937
There's so much I want
to talk to you about.

65
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:11,700
But first, why are you here?

66
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:14,300
It is a long and mundane tale.

67
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:17,397
But the first time I visited
was shortly after you left.

68
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:20,040
Since this was many years ago,

69
00:04:20,340 --> 00:04:24,620
both Ringo and nearby Hakumai
were held by the Shimotsuki.

70
00:04:24,980 --> 00:04:28,577
As you might recall, they were a
clan famed for their hardiness.

71
00:04:28,660 --> 00:04:31,900
The daimyo's name was
Lord Shimotsuki Ushimaru.

72
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:36,905
He was well known as a master swordsman
and always shared his company with a fox.

73
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:37,920
A fox?

74
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:44,820
But in the end, like every other region,
Ringo was lost to Kaido and his forces.

75
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:50,940
My lady, have you heard of the eternal
graves erected here as a local tradition?

76
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:52,510
Yes.

77
00:04:52,593 --> 00:04:54,217
Corpses are placed in caskets,

78
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:57,397
and they don't decompose for
centuries due to the cold.

79
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:58,540
That is correct.

80
00:04:58,740 --> 00:05:02,564
And their locations are marked by
swords stabbed into the ground.

81
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:05,978
People in Ringo are given
a blade when they are born.

82
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:10,546
They will grow up with them and
keep them into old age as well.

83
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:14,740
When they die, the swords they
carried serve as their grave markers.

84
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:18,520
For all time, they're
inseparable from their swords.

85
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:22,300
So, of course, that is why
they're called Eternal Graves.

86
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:27,544
Unfortunately, since some of these
weapons here are famed blades,

87
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:29,875
grave robbing is quite often an issue.

88
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:32,640
This is simply a fact of life in Ringo.

89
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:36,060
Back to my story.

90
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:39,800
Allow me to tell you what
transpired here 13 years ago.

91
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:53,280
Having lost you, I prepared to
slice open my belly in shame.

92
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,157
Dammit, what the hell is that thing?

93
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:05,800
It must be a monster!

94
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:09,760
Forget about the swords! Run away!

95
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:12,102
This must be some samurai curse!

96
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:19,460
What a nuisance.

97
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:21,280
I've come a long way.

98
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:23,206
At least let me die in peace.

99
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:32,260
I know you. That's right.

100
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:35,322
If my memory serves me,
it was several years ago.

101
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,937
You must be Onimaru, correct?

102
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:41,400
Indeed,

103
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:44,037
the Komofox that stood before me was the

104
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:46,740
loyal companion of Lord
Shimotsuki Ushimaru,

105
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:49,080
the late daimyo of Ringo.

106
00:06:58,860 --> 00:07:00,220
It can't be.

107
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:02,400
Oh, these graves.

108
00:07:02,780 --> 00:07:05,460
Have you been protecting them on your own?

109
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:09,629
More than five years had passed
since the downfall of Ringo.

110
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:10,737
And all that time,

111
00:07:10,820 --> 00:07:13,097
Onimaru alone had been
protecting the eternal

112
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:16,004
graves from thieves who
would take their swords.

113
00:07:16,660 --> 00:07:17,490
Here.

114
00:07:17,573 --> 00:07:19,020
No need to fear me.

115
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:21,020
I am your ally.

116
00:07:25,140 --> 00:07:26,120
I see.

117
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:27,440
You are injured.

118
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:35,430
Onimaru!

119
00:07:35,513 --> 00:07:37,160
Stay strong, my friend!

120
00:07:48,980 --> 00:07:49,810
Oh-ho!

121
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:51,700
So you're finally awake.

122
00:07:52,020 --> 00:07:53,500
Here, have some food.

123
00:07:53,940 --> 00:07:56,640
I've been told that
fox is like fried tofu.

124
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:00,870
Oh?

125
00:08:00,953 --> 00:08:02,232
Is something the matter?

126
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:04,797
You must eat, or your
wound will never heal.

127
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:07,917
Well, then how will you
protect your master's grave?

128
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,160
Don't be stubborn. Just take a bite.

129
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,040
I promise you'll like it.

130
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:13,600
You can trust me.

131
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:19,240
Ka-ba-ba!

132
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:22,192
Just a spot of indigestion, not to worry.

133
00:08:22,340 --> 00:08:24,811
The food was so good I ate a bit too much.

134
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,660
Ka-ba-ba-ba!

135
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:30,360
Never mind my belly's rumbling.

136
00:08:30,940 --> 00:08:33,000
Please, I do insist.

137
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:49,060
Oh, I knew it.

138
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,240
It is good.

139
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,751
I thought you might come.

140
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:30,000
We need not fight.

141
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:33,650
Forgive me.

142
00:09:33,733 --> 00:09:35,100
I know how you feel.

143
00:09:43,860 --> 00:09:44,940
Release me!

144
00:09:47,220 --> 00:09:50,380
I don't expect you to
understand why I'm doing this.

145
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:54,397
Trust me when I tell you I do not
want to disturb the peace of the dead.

146
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:58,360
But right now, I must,
or this land will suffer.

147
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:02,800
Leave to the future.

148
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:04,550
Live on.

149
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:19,677
The fight for this country isn't over.

150
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:22,680
In 13 years, there will
be another great battle.

151
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:33,777
The day will come when the
samurai of this nation rise

152
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:37,537
again Standing proud in the
face of our adversaries But

153
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:40,857
their efforts will not bear
fruit without swords A great

154
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:45,580
many of them On the field of
battle When your comrade falls,

155
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:51,497
you take up their blade And carry
on The souls that reside in those

156
00:10:51,580 --> 00:10:56,380
blades will empower the samurai
as they strike down their foes.

157
00:10:56,520 --> 00:11:00,580
Until that day is won, this
land is still a battlefield!

158
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:03,260
Listen to me, Onimaru.

159
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,957
The battle between the
beast pirates and the

160
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:09,080
people of the land of
Wano is not over yet.

161
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:12,777
It is still too early to
lay these swords to rest.

162
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:15,507
In preparation for the
return of the samurai,

163
00:11:15,620 --> 00:11:18,257
we must guard these swords and ensure that

164
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:20,457
the grave robbers don't take a single one,

165
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:21,370
all right?

166
00:11:22,020 --> 00:11:26,920
Therefore, I'll collect every
blade myself, and hide them away!

167
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:31,740
I understand now, I've failed at my duty!

168
00:11:32,180 --> 00:11:34,460
But I've been given a second chance!

169
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:37,980
This is the role I must fulfill!

170
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:44,360
Come back!

171
00:11:45,660 --> 00:11:47,260
Lady Hiyori!

172
00:11:56,800 --> 00:12:00,780
when i fail to protect lady hyori
i plan to end my life in shame

173
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:05,397
but i can't die yet not when there's

174
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:09,080
work to be done not when i can be of use

175
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:15,137
i have so much remorse if
i don't keep busy it will

176
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:19,980
consume me if you refuse to
let go Bite off my damned arm!

177
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:22,320
Take it and eat it for all I care!

178
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:25,960
But I will not give up until I'm through!

179
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:15,440
Oh, my Mario.

180
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:32,200
What is this?

181
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:34,797
So you've had a change of heart already?

182
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:37,292
Could it be that you understood my words?

183
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:41,100
I won't complain.

184
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:42,720
Let's work together.

185
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:44,950
Thus,

186
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:47,637
Onimaru and I joined forces
to protect the graves

187
00:13:47,720 --> 00:13:50,779
of the samurai and hide
their swords away for later.

188
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:03,740
All right, another day of robbing graves.

189
00:14:11,340 --> 00:14:13,580
Rather frigid this morning, isn't it?

190
00:14:15,940 --> 00:14:20,116
If it carries on like this, soon we
won't have any place left to sleep.

191
00:14:20,540 --> 00:14:23,599
Perhaps we could dig a bit
of a cavern to hide them?

192
00:14:27,320 --> 00:14:28,280
I'm famished.

193
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:32,138
If I sell a sword or two in
the capital, I could eat.

194
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:37,035
Imagine working on a full stomach and
not worrying about food every day.

195
00:14:37,900 --> 00:14:38,730
Onimaru.

196
00:14:41,300 --> 00:14:43,540
All in chest. Don't worry.

197
00:14:46,740 --> 00:14:49,860
And yet, an army marches on its stomach.

198
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:53,560
This is for the greater good.

199
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:55,080
Forgive me.

200
00:14:56,380 --> 00:14:58,000
I'm back, Onimaru.

201
00:14:58,380 --> 00:15:01,145
I brought some food for
the two of us to share.

202
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:03,276
Look, your favorite.

203
00:15:03,620 --> 00:15:04,580
Fried tofu.

204
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:06,190
Ooh!

205
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:14,755
I failed to see how we're
going to make money out here.

206
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:17,786
Bingo, are you sure this
plan's going to work?

207
00:15:18,180 --> 00:15:21,700
Yes, I did my research on
these so-called eternal graves.

208
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:23,520
They're a treasure Traffy.

209
00:15:23,620 --> 00:15:25,973
We can steal as many weapons as we like.

210
00:15:26,060 --> 00:15:26,890
You see that?

211
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:30,334
Cross that bridge, and we'll
reach a massive grave site.

212
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:33,017
Ka-pa-pa!

213
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:35,440
Ka-pa-pa-pa!

214
00:15:36,260 --> 00:15:37,201
Someone's there!

215
00:15:37,420 --> 00:15:38,900
Begone, you robbers!

216
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:42,580
You shall not seize a single
blade from the soul of Ringo!

217
00:15:42,880 --> 00:15:43,980
Not on my watch!

218
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:47,120
Bunch of nonsense! Bongo! Bongo! Attack!

219
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:49,030
Monimaru!

220
00:15:56,680 --> 00:15:58,300
What is all this?

221
00:15:58,420 --> 00:15:59,655
Who the hell are you?

222
00:15:59,940 --> 00:16:01,411
You want to know my name?

223
00:16:01,540 --> 00:16:03,020
Let me think.

224
00:16:04,180 --> 00:16:05,380
You don't know?

225
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:08,530
Hmm...

226
00:16:08,613 --> 00:16:09,700
Yes, perfect!

227
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:14,560
I am known as the Guardian
of Bandit's Bridge!

228
00:16:16,040 --> 00:16:16,870
Oh!

229
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:20,300
You, dear, mad love!

230
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:25,860
Now, leave your weapons and go!

231
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:27,400
Or face my wrath!

232
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:39,557
Yuki Maru, that can't be a coincidence.

233
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:41,700
Same name, doing the same job?

234
00:16:42,340 --> 00:16:44,040
To finish up the story,

235
00:16:44,320 --> 00:16:48,520
I went to the capital a short time
later in order to acquire some food.

236
00:16:48,700 --> 00:16:54,100
But after that, I was not able to return
to Ringo due to certain circumstances.

237
00:16:57,520 --> 00:17:00,200
CITIZENS OF THE CAPITAL,
PLEASE FORGIVE ME!

238
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:07,600
YOU'RE UNDER ARREST OF AN OPEN EDGE!

239
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:11,200
WE FINALLY CAUGHT YOU,
Belt FRIED TOEFU THIEVE!

240
00:17:11,380 --> 00:17:12,560
NOW STOP RESISTING!

241
00:17:13,420 --> 00:17:17,120
I'M A FULL, THIS IS THE
GRAVEST BLUNDER OF MY LIFE!

242
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:27,200
Forgive me, Onimaru.

243
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:33,760
And you were held captive for 13 years?

244
00:17:34,440 --> 00:17:36,120
I let everyone down.

245
00:17:36,820 --> 00:17:40,840
But wait, you're here because
you wanted to see that fox again?

246
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:42,060
Oh, no.

247
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:46,277
I'm sure if he's still alive that
Onimaru has given up on me by now.

248
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:48,320
It's been 13 years after all.

249
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:50,520
He must have felt betrayed.

250
00:17:58,840 --> 00:18:01,487
What happened to that
monk you were fighting?

251
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:02,840
I wish I knew.

252
00:18:03,140 --> 00:18:05,077
Last I saw, he went through this door.

253
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,897
But then he vanished into thin air.

254
00:18:06,980 --> 00:18:08,677
Wait, through that door you said?

255
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:09,917
But this is...

256
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:11,677
What, you know something I don't know?

257
00:18:11,760 --> 00:18:12,780
Where is he?

